        "original_id": "423bf88a-951a-577b-ba09-7ead08ec7b46",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Gopalpur Tussar Fabrics, shawls\n- Organizations: Government of India\n- Concepts: Geographical Indication tags, clothing, etymology\n\nFacts:\n- In 2009, the Government of India granted a Geographical Indication tag to Gopalpur Tussar Fabrics.\n- A shawl is a simple item of clothing worn loosely over the shoulders, upper body, and arms, and sometimes over the head.\n- The word \"shawl\" comes through Persian and Urdu \"shāl\" and may derive from Hindi \"duśālā,\" ultimately from Sanskrit \"śāṭī\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
